commit 4e2b80ff17784d6f547816bc13b76c58f52b2ab9
Author: Matt Merhar <mattmerhar@protonmail.com>
Date:   Sun Jun 28 21:40:03 2026 -0400

    airoha: fix HSUART baud calculations
    
    On the W1700K-2, where console is ttyS0, EFR32MG21 is ttyS1, and GPS is
    ttyS2, only console was working as expected.
    
    Before:
            Port  Requested Actual
            ttyS0 115200    115200
            ttyS1 230400    115200
            ttyS2 460800    921600
            ttyS2 230400    230400
    
    After:
            Port  Requested Actual
            ttyS0 115200    115200
            ttyS1 115200    115200
            ttyS2 115200    115200
            ttyS2 230400    230400
            ttyS2 460800    460800
            ttyS2 921600    921600
    
    Note that testing with the GPS shows only /1 and /2 work as expected
    for HSUART, even though /4 would in theory allow for the lower baud
    rates to be slightly more accurate.
    
    Additionally, refactor to use a proper set_divisor callback.
    
    Signed-off-by: Matt Merhar <mattmerhar@protonmail.com>

